  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> enters one corner <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> of an equilateral triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> wires of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> each and leaves by the corner <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The currents <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> in ampere is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/183f227d-b2fe-4945-bcf0-d68c5fda31fa-image.png\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 181px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
